        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Bon</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 100 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Origin</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>: Bonpos hold that it was taught in Olmo Lungring or Tazig, west of Tibet, and came first to Zhangzhung, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-kailash">Mount Kailash</a>, then to Tibet; scholars distinguish an ancient Bon of the era before 618 CE from a classical Yungdrung Bon of the 10th and 11th centuries.</span></div>
